__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-include tools/.
#
# The repository root .gitignore has a blanket `tools/` rule (line 20), aimed at
# scratch tooling elsewhere in the tree. It also matched cpp/gh200_sim/tools/,
# so dump_phi.cu, palmieri_centres.cpp and the initializer goldens were never
# committable -- while CMakeLists.txt declared `add_executable(dump_phi
# tools/dump_phi.cu)` unconditionally. The files existed on the author's disk,
# the build worked there, and every fresh clone died at CMake generate time with
# "Cannot find source file". That is the root cause of the branch never having
# been buildable, and it was invisible from inside a working copy.
#
# Un-ignoring a directory requires re-including the directory itself before its
# contents: git does not descend into an ignored directory to find negations.
!tools/
!tools/**
